Zendaya & Tom Holland Are Already Married, Stylist Law Roach Claims: &#8216;You Missed&nbsp;It&#8217;

Zendaya & the &#8216;Euphoria&#8217; Cast Face Harsh Realities of Adulthood in Long-Awaited Season 3&nbsp;Trailer

&#8216;Stunningly Realistic&#8217; Zendaya Wax Figure Featuring Tom Holland Engagement Ring&nbsp;Unveiled

After the fashion expert shocked fans by claiming that the famous couple&#8217;s nuptials had &#8220;already happened&#8221; in a red-carpet interview at the Actor Awards, Stoermer reportedly reposted a clip of the moment on her Instagram Story. &#8220;The laugh….,&#8221; she wrote in a since-deleted post, according to Entertainment Weekly .

The Actor Awards took place Sunday (March 1). At the event, Law bluntly told an Access Hollywood reporter who&#8217;d asked about Zendaya and the Marvel actor&#8217;s wedding, &#8220;You missed it.&#8221;

&#8220;It&#8217;s very true,&#8221; he added at the time when the surprised journalist sought confirmation.

Billboard previously reached out to the two stars&#8217; reps and the stylist for comment.

The Challengers star is the daughter of Stoermer and Kazembe Ajamu Coleman, who both worked as school teachers in Zendaya&#8217;s hometown of Oakland, Calif. In 2016, reports emerged that the Disney Channel alum&#8217;s mom had filed for divorce after eight years of marriage, which Zendaya confirmed by sharing a then-recent family photo on X and writing, &#8220;My parents ain&#8217;t been together for a long time, y&#8217;all didn&#8217;t know cause we private+they still homies #lateassnews.&#8221;

A decade later, the Euphoria leading lady still prefers to keep her personal life private &#8212; as evidenced by the confusion over her possibly marrying Holland without the public knowing. The pair have always kept their relationship low-key, getting engaged around the beginning of 2025 but not confirming it until that September, when Holland corrected a reporter who&#8217;d called Zendaya his &#8220;girlfriend&#8221; instead of his &#8220;fiancée.&#8221;
